#. box title
#: site/lectures/12-oop-nomenclatures.md:1463
msgid "Inheritance or a new field?"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-oop-nomenclatures.md:1464
msgid "Inherit when the new kind **is a** nomenclature that works differently (bands) or has more (parents). Do not inherit just to reuse two lines of code - a function or a module does that. Deep chains of subclasses are hard to follow; one level is usually enough."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-oop-nomenclatures.md:1471
msgid "Make a `BandedNomenclature` for the size of a loan: `small` below 50,000, `medium` below 1,000,000, `large` from 1,000,000. Apply it to the outstanding amounts of `loans.csv` and count the loans per size."
